LICENSING TERMS FOR THIS DATASET
================================

This dataset (the "Dataset") is not distributed under a single licence. It
comprises three categories of content, each originating from a different rights
holder and each remaining subject to its own terms. Any person who reproduces,
redistributes, or otherwise makes use of any portion of the Dataset (the
"Recipient") is required to review these terms in full beforehand, and to observe
the terms applicable to each category of content they use.

Summary of terms. The contributions of the authors are licensed under CC BY 4.0.
Excerpts quoted from third-party works remain subject to the licence recorded in
the `license` field of each excerpt record. Because a portion of those excerpts is
licensed on NonCommercial terms, and a further portion on NoDerivatives terms, the
Dataset as distributed is NOT available for commercial use, and no provision of
this file should be construed as granting such rights. A Recipient requiring a
commercially usable subset may obtain one by excluding every excerpt whose
`license` field contains "-NC", together with those containing "-ND" where
modification of excerpt text is intended. This summary is provided for convenience
and does not limit or vary the terms of the sections below.


1. ANNOTATIONS, QUERIES, AND STRUCTURE — CC BY 4.0
---
Copyright (c) 2026 the authors. All material identified in this Section is
licensed to the Recipient under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International Public Licence (CC BY 4.0), the full text of which is available at
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. This Section applies to the
following, each of which is the original work of the authors:

  - annotations_scoring.jsonl and annotations_verification.jsonl in their
    entirety (per-rater harm scores, support votes, means, PCM aggregates);
  - queries.jsonl in its entirety, and the `query` and `topic` fields wherever
    they appear;
  - the segmentation of model answers into segments, the decomposition into
    claims, the citation-match statuses, the licence tiering, and every derived
    field in segments.jsonl;

Nothing in this Section extends to the material governed by Sections 2 and 3.


2. QUOTED EXCERPTS — each under its source article's own licence
---
The Dataset incorporates excerpts quoted from articles published on PubMed
Central. These excerpts are the works of third parties. The authors neither own
nor purport to license them, and grant no rights in respect of them. The licence
governing each excerpt is recorded in the `license` field of its record, and the
licences so recorded include Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY),
Attribution-NonCommercial (CC BY-NC), Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives
(CC BY-NC-ND), Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike (CC BY-NC-SA) and
Attribution-NoDerivatives (CC BY-ND), in various versions, together with works
dedicated under CC0 and works under the UK Open Government Licence.

A Recipient who reproduces or redistributes any excerpt does so subject to the
licence recorded for that excerpt, and is responsible for attributing the source
article. The fields `source_title`, `source_authors`, `source_journal`,
`source_year`, `source_url` and `license` are provided on every record for that
purpose.

Where an excerpt could not be delivered, its `excerpt` field is null and no other
field describes it. In respect of such an excerpt the Dataset publishes no part of
the passage and no description of it, and the authors make no representation as 
to its content or extent. What remains is a citation to the source article, together 
with the authors' own record of how that citation was made. A Recipient who obtains 
the text of such an excerpt from any other source holds it subject to the terms of
the source article, and nothing in this file grants any right in it.

Where the `verbatim` field of an excerpt record is false, the text distributed is
the language model's rendering and not the wording of the source article. Such
text shall not be attributed to the source article as a quotation.


3. MODEL-GENERATED TEXT — provider terms apply
---
The `text` field of each segment, and the `claims` derived from it, are the output
of six commercial and open-weight language models: Claude Opus 4.6, DeepSeek V3.2,
Gemini 3.1 Pro, GPT-5.4, Mistral Small 2603, and Qwen 3.5 397B. The `model` field
of each segment record identifies the model from which that segment originates.

The authors assert no copyright in this material and grant no rights in respect of
it. The terms of service of the respective providers may restrict the use that may
be made of model output, including in several instances its use in training or
improving competing models. A Recipient whose intended use depends on rights in
this material is responsible for ascertaining and complying with the terms of the
applicable provider.


WARRANTY
---
THE DATASET IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS
FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, ACCURACY, AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
AUTHORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN
ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT, OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF, OR IN CONNECTION
WITH THE DATASET OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE DATASET.

The licence classification recorded for each excerpt reflects metadata resolved
from the NCBI E-utilities and the PMC Open Access service at the time of
compilation. It is provided in good faith, may contain errors, and does not
constitute legal advice. A Recipient intending to rely on that classification is
responsible for verifying it against the source article.


